Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the packaging business in the United States and internationally. It operates through Americas Beverage, European Beverage, Asia Pacific, and Transit Packaging segments. The company manufactures and sells recyclable aluminum beverage cans and ends, glass bottles, steel crowns, aluminum caps, non-beverage cans, food and aerosol cans, and ends and closures. It provides manual, semi-automatic, and automatic equipment and tools to apply and remove consumables, such as straps and films; protective solutions, including airbags, edge protectors, and honeycomb products; and steel and plastic consumables include steel strap, plastic strap, industrial film, and other related products. It serves food industries, including pet food, personal care, household, and industrial products. Crown Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1892 and is headquartered in Tampa, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Timothy J. Donahue | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 62 | Compensation: $5.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 23K people. Revenue per employee of $538K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $49K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Crown Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $13.1B market cap on $12.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 7% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.08892058963385523},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2402175.0},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 41% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (CCK) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Understanding_the_Setup:_CCK_and_Scalable_Risk_111026092601_1794320761.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794320761.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Crown Holdings (CCK) Following Its Strong Run Is The Undervalued Case Still There","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-cck/crown-holdings/news/crown-holdings-cck-following-its-strong-run-is-the-undervalu","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794208818.236,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.92,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's Why Crown Holdings (CCK) is a Strong Momentum Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025528/here-s-why-crown-holdings-cck-is-a-strong-momentum-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3025528","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ranpak (NYSE:PACK) and Crown (NYSE:CCK) Head to Head Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/ranpak-nysepack-and-crown-nysecck-head-to-head-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793899037.0,"or